{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7c1f4e2-5a3d-4e77-9f10-0c2a8d61e4a1",
    "name": "Account Notification API (Core ↔ Lending)",
    "description": "# Account Notification API\n\nHow the **core banking system (CBS)** tells the **lending platform** that money moved on an account it was asked to watch, and how the lending platform tells the core which accounts to watch.\n\nEverything here is generic: hosts, tokens, account numbers and amounts are collection variables, so the same collection can be pointed at any environment (local, UAT, production) without editing a request.\n\n---\n\n## The flow\n\n```\n  Lending platform                          Core banking system\n        |                                           |\n        |  1. POST /bulk  (accounts to watch)       |\n        | ----------------------------------------> |\n        |                                           |\n        |                                     ( account moves:\n        |                                       credit or debit )\n        |                                           |\n        |  2. POST /api/cbs/notifications/credit    |\n        | <---------------------------------------- |\n        |                                           |\n        |  3. 200 { notificationId, status }        |\n        | ----------------------------------------> |\n        |                                           |\n        |  4. DELETE /delete/{accountNumber}        |\n        | ----------------------------------------> |\n```\n\n1. **Register** — the lending platform posts the account numbers it wants monitored.\n2. **Notify** — every time one of those accounts moves, the core posts a notification to the lending platform's listener. This is the payload this collection is really about: folder *1. Core → Lending*.\n3. **Acknowledge** — the listener always answers `200` with a `notificationId` and a `status`, unless the token is wrong (`401`) or the body is not JSON (`400`). The core does not need to interpret the `status`; a `200` means the notification was captured.\n4. **Deregister** — when an account no longer needs watching.\n\n---\n\n## Authentication\n\n| Direction | Header | Variable |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Core → Lending | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` **or** `x-cbs-token: <token>` | `{{inboundToken}}` |\n| Lending → Core | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (Basic also supported) | `{{coreAuthToken}}` |\n\nThe inbound token is a single shared secret. If the listener is configured without one, the token check is skipped entirely — useful for a sandbox, never for production.\n\n---\n\n## Identifiers and idempotency\n\n| Field | Who sets it | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `externalReference` | core | The core's own transaction reference. **This is the deduplication key** — re-delivering the same reference returns the original notification instead of creating a second one. It is unique across the whole listener, so it must be globally unique per transaction, not per account. |\n| `correlationId` | core (optional) | Free-form trace id carried through the logs. When absent the listener generates one. |\n| `notificationId` | lending platform | Returned in the acknowledgement. Quote this when chasing a notification. |\n\nA core that cannot guarantee a unique `externalReference` should omit it — every delivery is then stored as a distinct notification, including genuine retries.\n\n---\n\n## Retry expectations\n\nThe listener answers `200` even when it could not act on a notification (unknown account, bad amount) — the `status` field carries that outcome, and the record is kept for inspection and manual retry on the lending side. The core should therefore retry only on a transport failure, a `5xx`, or a timeout, and it should reuse the same `externalReference` when it does.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{inboundToken}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Give every run a fresh transaction reference and timestamp, so repeated",
          "// runs read as new transactions rather than replays of an earlier one.",
          "// The replay request deliberately ignores these and reuses the last one.",
          "const stamp = Date.now();",
          "const noise = Math.floor(Math.random() * 100000).toString().padStart(5, '0');",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('externalReference', 'TXN' + stamp + noise);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('notifiedAt', new Date().toISOString());"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "lendingBaseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:9002", "type": "string", "description": "Host of the lending platform that receives notifications." },
    { "key": "coreBaseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080/api/v1/notification", "type": "string", "description": "Base path of the core banking notification API." },
    { "key": "inboundToken", "value": "replace-with-shared-inbound-token", "type": "string", "description": "Shared secret the core presents when posting a notification." },
    { "key": "coreAuthToken", "value": "replace-with-core-api-token", "type": "string", "description": "Token the lending platform presents to the core." },
    { "key": "accountNumber", "value": "1000123456789", "type": "string", "description": "The monitored account." },
    { "key": "secondAccountNumber", "value": "1000987654321", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "providerId", "value": "PRO0001", "type": "string", "description": "Provider / channel code issued by the core." },
    { "key": "accountCategory", "value": "SAVING", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "currency", "value": "ETB", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accountMinimumBalance", "value": "25", "type": "string", "description": "Balance the account must retain." },
    { "key": "creditAmount", "value": "1500.00", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "balanceAfterCredit", "value": "1725.50", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "debitAmount", "value": "400.00", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "balanceAfterDebit", "value": "1325.50", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "externalReference", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Set per run by the collection pre-request script." },
    { "key": "notifiedAt", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Set per run by the collection pre-request script." },
    { "key": "lastExternalReference", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Captured from the last accepted notification, so the replay request can reuse it." },
    { "key": "lastNotificationId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminSessionCookie", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Session cookie for the operator endpoint in folder 3." }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Core → Lending · Account activity notifications",
      "description": "The core posts one request per movement on a monitored account. Same endpoint, same envelope, whether the money went in or out — the payload says which.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST {{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit`\n\n### Payload\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `accountNumber` | string | **yes** | The monitored account the movement happened on. |\n| `amount` | number \\| numeric string | **yes** | Magnitude of the movement, always positive. The direction is carried by `transactionType`, not by the sign. |\n| `transactionType` | string | no | `CREDIT` or `DEBIT`. |\n| `currentBalance` | number | no | Account balance **after** the movement. |\n| `accountMinimumBalance` | number | no | Balance the account must retain. |\n| `accountCategory` | string | no | Account classification from the core. |\n| `externalReference` | string | no | Core's transaction reference; the deduplication key. |\n| `correlationId` | string | no | Trace id. |\n| `providerId` | string | no | Provider / channel code. |\n| `notifiedAt` | ISO-8601 string | no | When the core raised the notification. |\n\nAny additional field the core wants to send is accepted and stored with the notification verbatim, so the payload can be extended without a change on the lending side.\n\n### Acknowledgement\n\n```json\n{ \"notificationId\": \"<id>\", \"status\": \"<outcome>\", \"message\": \"<human readable>\" }\n```\n\n`status` is the listener's own processing outcome — `PENDING`, `DUPLICATE`, `UNMATCHED_ACCOUNT`, `FAILED` or a terminal status. It is diagnostic information for the lending side; for the core, a `200` means the notification was captured either way.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Credit — money into the account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "A deposit, transfer in, or any other inbound movement on a monitored account.\n\n`currentBalance` is the balance **after** the credit has landed. Send it post-settlement: a pre-credit snapshot understates what is on the account and makes the notification look smaller than the movement really was.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"{{externalReference}}\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": {{creditAmount}},\n  \"currency\": \"{{currency}}\",\n  \"currentBalance\": {{balanceAfterCredit}},\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": {{accountMinimumBalance}},\n  \"accountCategory\": \"{{accountCategory}}\",\n  \"providerId\": \"{{providerId}}\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"{{notifiedAt}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Acknowledged with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Acknowledgement carries a notificationId', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('notificationId');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Remember this delivery so the replay request can resend it verbatim.",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastExternalReference', pm.collectionVariables.get('externalReference'));",
                  "if (body.notificationId) pm.collectionVariables.set('lastNotificationId', body.notificationId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Captured",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"5f1c6b2a-9d4e-4c31-b0a7-8e2f4d6c1b90\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"TXN175823940012345\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"1000123456789\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": 1500.00,\n  \"currency\": \"ETB\",\n  \"currentBalance\": 1725.50,\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": 25,\n  \"accountCategory\": \"SAVING\",\n  \"providerId\": \"PRO0001\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"2026-09-16T08:41:22.318Z\"\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"notificationId\": \"clx9k2p0a0001qz8v7m3n5t2y\",\n  \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n  \"message\": \"Notification received.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Debit — money out of the account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "A withdrawal, transfer out, or any other outbound movement on a monitored account.\n\nSame endpoint and same envelope as a credit. Two things differ:\n\n- `transactionType` is `DEBIT`;\n- `currentBalance` is **lower** than before the movement.\n\n`amount` stays positive — it is the size of the movement, not a signed ledger entry. The pair `transactionType` + `currentBalance` is what tells the lending side which way the money went and where the account landed.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"{{externalReference}}\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"DEBIT\",\n  \"amount\": {{debitAmount}},\n  \"currency\": \"{{currency}}\",\n  \"currentBalance\": {{balanceAfterDebit}},\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": {{accountMinimumBalance}},\n  \"accountCategory\": \"{{accountCategory}}\",\n  \"providerId\": \"{{providerId}}\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"{{notifiedAt}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Acknowledged with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Acknowledgement carries a notificationId', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('notificationId');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Captured",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"a4d70e18-2b55-4f0c-9a31-6c5b8e7d2a44\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"TXN175823940198765\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"1000123456789\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"DEBIT\",\n  \"amount\": 400.00,\n  \"currency\": \"ETB\",\n  \"currentBalance\": 1325.50,\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": 25,\n  \"accountCategory\": \"SAVING\",\n  \"providerId\": \"PRO0001\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"2026-09-16T09:02:10.774Z\"\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"notificationId\": \"clx9k3r7b0004qz8v2h8k9p1c\",\n  \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n  \"message\": \"Notification received.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Credit — minimum payload",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "The smallest body the listener accepts: which account, and how much moved.\n\nUse it to confirm connectivity and the shared token before wiring up the full payload. Note what is lost by sending only this — with no `externalReference` there is no deduplication, and with no `currentBalance` the listener knows the movement but not the resulting position of the account.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n  \"amount\": {{creditAmount}}\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Acknowledged with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Captured",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumber\": \"1000123456789\",\n  \"amount\": 1500.00\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"notificationId\": \"clx9k4s9c0007qz8v5d2m7r3e\",\n  \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n  \"message\": \"Notification received.\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Replay — same transaction delivered twice",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "Resends the `externalReference` from the last accepted notification — what happens when the core retries after a timeout, or when the same transaction is published twice.\n\nRun **Credit — money into the account** first; this request reuses the reference that request captured.\n\nThe listener recognises the reference and returns the **original** `notificationId` rather than creating a second record. This is why `externalReference` must be unique per transaction across all accounts: it is the only thing standing between a network retry and a double-counted movement.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"{{lastExternalReference}}\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": {{creditAmount}},\n  \"currency\": \"{{currency}}\",\n  \"currentBalance\": {{balanceAfterCredit}},\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": {{accountMinimumBalance}},\n  \"accountCategory\": \"{{accountCategory}}\",\n  \"providerId\": \"{{providerId}}\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"{{notifiedAt}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Acknowledged with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Resolves to the original notification, not a new one', () => {",
                  "    const previous = pm.collectionVariables.get('lastNotificationId');",
                  "    if (previous) pm.expect(pm.response.json().notificationId).to.eql(previous);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Recognised as a replay",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"7c2e9a13-6f84-4b02-8d5a-1e3c7b9f0d26\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"TXN175823940012345\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"1000123456789\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": 1500.00,\n  \"currency\": \"ETB\",\n  \"currentBalance\": 1725.50,\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": 25,\n  \"accountCategory\": \"SAVING\",\n  \"providerId\": \"PRO0001\",\n  \"notifiedAt\": \"2026-09-16T08:41:22.318Z\"\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"notificationId\": \"clx9k2p0a0001qz8v7m3n5t2y\",\n  \"status\": \"DUPLICATE\",\n  \"message\": \"Notification already processed (status=PENDING).\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Rejected — incomplete payload",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "A payload with no `accountNumber`.\n\nThe listener answers **`200`, not `4xx`** — the notification is stored with `status: \"FAILED\"` and the reason, so a malformed delivery is visible and inspectable on the lending side rather than lost. The core should treat this as delivered and **not** retry it; only transport errors, `5xx` and timeouts are worth retrying.\n\nSame outcome for a non-numeric or negative `amount`.\n\nThe second saved example shows the one body-level case that does return `4xx`: a request that is not JSON at all.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"{{externalReference}}\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": {{creditAmount}},\n  \"providerId\": \"{{providerId}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Still acknowledged with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Outcome is reported in the body', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('FAILED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Stored as FAILED",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"1b8d3f60-4a27-4e95-9c02-5d6a8b1e7f34\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"TXN175823940155512\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": 1500.00,\n  \"providerId\": \"PRO0001\"\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"notificationId\": \"clx9k5t2d000aqz8v8j4n6w5f\",\n  \"status\": \"FAILED\",\n  \"message\": \"Invalid payload: accountNumber and positive amount are required.\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "400 · Body is not JSON",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
                  "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "accountNumber=1000123456789&amount=1500",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "text" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "Bad Request",
              "code": 400,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"error\": \"Invalid JSON body\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Rejected — wrong or missing token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "not-the-shared-token", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{lendingBaseUrl}}/api/cbs/notifications/credit",
              "host": ["{{lendingBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "cbs", "notifications", "credit"]
            },
            "description": "The listener rejects the delivery before reading the body and stores nothing.\n\nThe token may be presented either way:\n\n- `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n- `x-cbs-token: <token>`\n\nA `401` here means a configuration mismatch, not a bad transaction — the core should alert rather than retry in a loop.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"correlationId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"externalReference\": \"{{externalReference}}\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n  \"transactionType\": \"CREDIT\",\n  \"amount\": {{creditAmount}},\n  \"currentBalance\": {{balanceAfterCredit}},\n  \"accountMinimumBalance\": {{accountMinimumBalance}},\n  \"providerId\": \"{{providerId}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Rejected with 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
