    {
      "name": "2. Lending → Core · Which accounts to watch",
      "description": "The other half of the contract: nothing is notified until an account is on the core's watch list, and notifications keep coming until it is taken off.\n\nBoth calls live under `{{coreBaseUrl}}` and authenticate with `{{coreAuthToken}}` (Bearer, or HTTP Basic where the core requires it).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register accounts for monitoring",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{coreAuthToken}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{coreBaseUrl}}/bulk",
              "host": ["{{coreBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["bulk"]
            },
            "description": "Adds account numbers to the core's watch list. From this point the core posts a notification on every movement on those accounts.\n\nThe call is **additive and idempotent** — an account already on the list is counted under `alreadyExistsCount` rather than duplicated, so the whole list can safely be re-sent on a schedule.\n\nThe core caps the list per request (commonly 1000 accounts); longer lists are split across several calls and the counts summed.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumbers\": [\n    \"{{accountNumber}}\",\n    \"{{secondAccountNumber}}\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Registered",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{coreBaseUrl}}/bulk",
                  "host": ["{{coreBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["bulk"]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumbers\": [\n    \"1000123456789\",\n    \"1000987654321\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"totalReceived\": 2,\n  \"insertedCount\": 1,\n  \"alreadyExistsCount\": 1\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Stop monitoring an account",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{coreAuthToken}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{coreBaseUrl}}/delete/{{accountNumber}}",
              "host": ["{{coreBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["delete", "{{accountNumber}}"]
            },
            "description": "Takes one account off the watch list; no more notifications are raised for it.\n\nThe account number goes in the path and must be URL-encoded. Removing an account that is not on the list is not an error."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 · Removed",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "DELETE",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{coreBaseUrl}}/delete/1000123456789",
                  "host": ["{{coreBaseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["delete", "1000123456789"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
